\begin{definition}
\label{def:6-38-extra-1}



A set $A \subseteq \mathbb{R}^n$ has measure zero if, for every $\delta>0$, there is a countable collection of open rectangles covering $A$ whose volumes sum to less than $\delta$.
\end{definition}

